# Applies to every Docker build in this repo (ADR-0001 §5.4: "must exclude").
# Default-deny for anything that is project data, a secret, or VCS/editor
# noise. Add new source directories to the allow-list in each Dockerfile's
# COPY step, not by loosening this file.

# Secrets — never in any image (ADR-0001 §5.4, §9 S1/S4)
# Bare patterns match only at the build-context root under this repo's
# BuildKit, not recursively (same gotcha the Python-artifacts section below
# already documents for **/__pycache__/) -- verified empirically via a
# disposable Docker build context with nested secrets/data files, both
# with and without the **/ prefix (docs/ops audit, 2026-08-09). The
# allow-list negations must be equally recursive or a real nested template
# (deploy/compose/.env.example) is wrongly excluded once the secret pattern
# above it is corrected.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.*.example

# Project data / governance ledgers — INV-1: no container touches project data
data/
research/data/
research/evidence_library/
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3

# VCS / CI / editor
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Python artifacts
# Docker (unlike .gitignore) does not match a bare "dirname/" recursively —
# it must be prefixed with "**/" to exclude at any depth. Verified empirically
# (docker build + `find /app -iname __pycache__` inside the built image)
# during this image's own build-verification pass.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
venv/
.venv/

# Local build logs and launchers (repo-root clutter, not image inputs)
run_*.bat
corpus_build*.log
corpus_build*.err*
perp_build*.log
perp_build*.err*
h1_build*.log
h1_build*.err*
h4_build*.log
h4_build*.err*
h5_build*.log
h5_build*.err*
h6_build*.log
h6_build*.err*
h6_validation*.log
h6_validation*.err*

# Regenerable research report output (research/reports/ — see .gitignore)
research/reports/

# Local-only project instructions, not needed inside any image
CLAUDE.md
